Here are the Firebase Security Rules required to allow users to update their own profile picture (and other profile fields). These rules ensure that a user can only write to the document in the `users` collection that matches their own Auth UID.

```javascript
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    // Allow anyone to read user profiles
    match /users/{userId} {
      allow read: if true;

      // Only allow the authenticated user to update their own profile
      allow write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
    }

    // ... rules for other collections ...
  }
}
```

